  "problem": "A study conducted on $3\\,400$ teenagers by the transportation department of a particular city reveals that teenagers' preference for the type of home-to-school transportation changes with time. The following table shows the results of this study.  \n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Bus** | **Bicycle** | **Electric Scooter ** |\n| To: | **Bus** | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n| **Bicycle** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ |  |\n| **Electric Scooter** | $0.4$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ |  |\n\nFor example, $40%$ of teenagers who used to go to school by bus now go by bicycle.  \n\nHow many teenagers would eventually go to school on electric scooters if the listed probabilities remained constant over many years?",
